|> 	I've been fooling around with Nethack 3.1 on MS-DOS and I
|> always play a knight.  Each time he dies (which is soon, of course) it
|> tells me he could jump.  But any time I try to make him jump, I get
|> "Illegal move."  I press 'j' and it asks me where I want to jump to, I
|> move the cursor one space away and press '.' and it tells me "Illegal
|> move."  Can he really jump or is this a bug?  Or am I doing this
|> wrong?
|> 	Thanks.

Knights are the only character that can jump, but only like chess moves.

(eg)

          .X.X.
          X...X   K = knight, . = floor, X = floor where knight can
          ..K..                              jump to.
          X...X
          .X.X.   (look in the chess rules)

